course: dictionary
lesson: 10663
title: Words of the law
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: The word unlawfully is made of three parts: un- means not, law is the rule a country or city makes, and -ly tells you it is an adverb, a word that says how something is done. So unlawfully means in a way that is not allowed by the law. You can check this by swapping in your meaning: «The fans were killed in a way that broke the law» still makes sense.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «At the Hillsborough disaster in 1989, 97 Liverpool fans died in a crush; inquests in 2016 found they were unlawfully killed and that the fans were not to blame.» The sentence says the fans were not to blame. So the word unlawfully tells you that someone broke the law when the fans died.
explain: News, law and history books use this word a lot. You may also read «unlawfully detained», which means held somewhere without the legal right to hold you, or «entered the country unlawfully», which means came into a country against its laws. Each time, the word warns the reader that a rule was broken.
fact: Unlawfully means in a way that is against the law.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so unlawful means not lawful.
fact: «Unlawfully» is an adverb, because it tells you how an action was done.
fact: «Unlawfully» often appears in news and history, where people explain that a rule was broken.
fact: The opposite of unlawfully is lawfully, which means in a way that follows the law.
exercise: «The fans were unlawfully killed, the inquests found.» What does unlawfully mean here? | In a very quick and sudden way | *In a way that is against the law | With great care and kindness | In a loud and angry way
exercise: «They entered the country unlawfully.» Find the one word that tells you the action broke the law. | country | entered | the | *unlawfully
exercise: Which word means the opposite of unlawfully? | *Lawfully | Loudly | Quickly | Rudely
test: The word un- at the start of unlawfully means what? | Very | *Not | Again | Before
test: In «The man was unlawfully detained», what does unlawfully suggest? | *Someone broke the law by holding him | He was in a hurry to leave | He was given a prize | He was fast asleep
exam: In «The fans were unlawfully killed», which word means the same as unlawfully? | Quietly | Lazily | *Illegally | Happily
